# Large, fully re-fetchable/regenerable data - regenerate with the
# scripts in Fetch/ instead of committing. AR5 additionally requires
# personal/organizational access (see README) - AR50 is the fully
# public fallback either way.
Data/OpenS_data/ar5_skog_national.gpkg
Data/OpenS_data/ar5_myr_national.gpkg
Data/OpenS_data/ar50_skog_national.gpkg
Data/OpenS_data/ar50_myr_national.gpkg
Data/OpenS_data/osm_buildings_national.gpkg
Data/OpenS_data/nin_data/
Data/OpenS_data/disturbance/
Data/OpenS_data/bioclim/
Data/OpenS_data/dtm1_coverage_union.gpkg

# Intermediate caches derived from the above - small themselves, but
# only meaningful alongside whichever source (AR5/AR50) built them
# (see the population_source column/tag). Not real deliverables; the
# actual results are the final index/map exports in Results/.
Data/OpenS_data/vegHeights_skog_climZoneRegion_openS.csv
Data/OpenS_data/vaatmark_pop_openS.gpkg
Data/OpenS_data/refvaatmark_NINA_median/

# Quick-test artifacts - not real results, and *.real_backup files are
